body:
The distributed agent-builder agent template opencode-suite/agents/agent-builder.md (product source embedded into the apg binary via include_str! and installed by apg init into ~/.opencode/agents/) offers and generates the agent roster the suite supports, and the optional coordinator has zero place in it — a mode: primary agent named in the template's roster and generated nowhere, so every mention is absent:
- the frontmatter description: (line 2) drops ", and an optional coordinator";
- the roster intro (lines 55-65) drops "and an optional coordinator", so the generated set is implementers only — the core/root implementer, per-subsystem <name>-implementers, and tiered test-implementers where a test tier is file-separable;
- the ### coordinator (optional) section (lines 274-276) is absent;
- workflow step 3's interview bullet "Whether a coordinator is wanted." (line 379) is absent;
- workflow step 4 (lines 381-383) names zero optional coordinator in the default plan;
- workflow step 5's scaffold line (line 385) reads mode: subagent unconditionally — the (optional coordinator: primary) branch is absent;
- non-negotiable rule 8 (line 335) drops "and coordinator" from its example of generated names that need explicit navigator-allowlist entries.

IMPORTANT: the coordinator targeted here is the OPTIONAL GENERATED PRIMARY AGENT, rather than the coordinator ROLE the codebase-navigator performs in the feedback-routing / task-cadence prose. Every use of the word coordinator for that role stays unchanged.

Acceptance criteria:
- opencode-suite/agents/agent-builder.md contains zero offer or generation of an optional coordinator agent: zero ### coordinator (optional) section, zero whether-a-coordinator-is-wanted interview bullet, zero primary-mode scaffold branch, and zero coordinator example in rule 8.
- Every generated agent is scaffolded mode: subagent.
- Scope is the one product-source file; the repo's own .opencode/agents/** are consumer artifacts and are untouched. Zero binary change.
- The rest of the template (permission-shape rules, gate rules, the register/verify steps) stays unchanged by THIS requirement.
